edium", "notes": ["Open seat: John Cornyn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Texas's open Senate seat has become one of the most competitive races of 2026 after Ken Paxton defeated incumbent John Cornyn in the Republican runoff. Democrat James Talarico has led most recent polls by two to six points, with the polling average around three points, though some Republican-leaning surveys show the race tied or slightly behind. Prediction markets give Talarico roughly a two-in-three chance of winning.\n\nMoney has flowed at record levels: Talarico has raised nearly $69 million and holds a large cash advantage, while Paxton has faced tens of millions in outside spending against him despite a strong third quarter of his own. Expert raters split between Tossup and Lean D, reflecting a genuinely close race in a state that normally favors Republicans.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6697, "margin": 2.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6924, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7255, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6997, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6523, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6444, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6983, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7151, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7008, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6832, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7125, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7022, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.6}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6724, "margin": 2.8}]}